<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela fund sells Seguros Banvalor for $1.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Venezuela fund sells Seguros Banvalor for $1.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan State Deposits Guarantee Fund (Fogade) sold insurance company Seguros Banvalor Thursday for 600 million bolivars ($1.3 million) to private investor Leopoldo Castillo Bozo, Fogade said.</p>
<p>Castillo Bozo's bid -- three times Banvalor's base price -- beat out four other investment groups.</p>
<p>Fogade inherited Banvalor when the government took over Banco Barinas in June 1994.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
